{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION to the previous comment: three symbol names were stripped from it by a shell-quoting error on my side (backticks ran as command substitution). Full text below; disregard the mangled version above.\n\nSTACK IS PHYSICALLY INVALID MID-CHAIN — this needs a landing-strategy decision, not another rebase.\n\nMEASURED runner.py at each stack position after rebasing onto current main (whose runner.py is now 798 LOC, up ~100 since this epic began):\n  7468=795   f184=802 (OVER the 800 hard cap)   dc0d=815 (OVER)   2682=670\n  2932=713   9249=713   281f=713 (all OVER 2682's attested <700 headroom test)   3a98=680\nThis matches the vote board exactly: 1012/1032/1081 green; 1014/1023/1043/1048/1067 Verified -1.\n\nThe chain GROWS runner.py before it SPLITS it. Against the old main (~698) that was fine; against 798 the early changes breach immediately. Two distinct gates fire: the 800-LOC CI hard cap (f184, dc0d) and 2682's own <700 headroom test (2932, 9249, 281f).\n\nREORDERING DOES NOT WORK — attempted and aborted cleanly (backup ref kept, S5's in-progress work stashed and restored, nothing lost). Two hard dependencies block it:\n  (a) 2682 cannot precede dc0d. Its split captured the POST-dc0d signature of the structured-run helper (the one taking the capability record rather than the resolved model string), so applying it earlier puts the newer-signature function into the extracted module while runner.py still calls the older form.\n  (b) 3a98 cannot precede 2682, because it moves code INTO the module that 2682 creates.\nSo BOTH shrinking changes are pinned AFTER the growing ones. The projected clean ordering (795/650/617/624/637/680/680/680) is unreachable without re-authoring closed stories' commits.\n\nOPTIONS, none to be taken silently:\n1. FEATURE BRANCH — the project's own documented answer for multi-story work (CONTRIBUTING.md section 4: \"not one giant change or a fragile chain\"). Each story is reviewed into a server-side feature branch, then ONE no-fast-forward merge change goes into main. CI gates the MERGE, so intermediate LOC states never gate. Requires feature-branch-driver rights, which the bot identity may not hold.\n2. RE-AUTHOR 2682 to split against the pre-dc0d runner.py, then reorder. Substantial surgery on a CLOSED story's commit, and it would invalidate that story's attestation.\n3. SHRINK runner.py inside 7468 by ~20 lines so f184 (802) and dc0d (815) fit under 800. Needs another movable seam in the FIRST change; providers.py, which 7468 creates, is at 299/300 and cannot absorb it.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: option 1. It is the documented mechanism for exactly this situation, it is the only option that does not re-author closed stories, and at 8 changes deep this is precisely the fragility the feature-branch flow exists to avoid."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785459089425924001,"uuid":"f4883aff-947f-4128-8112-3172fc54c4b6"}